# Contributing to {{REPO_NAME}}

Read first: `../{{DOCS_REPO}}/docs/onboarding.md`, then `AGENTS.md`, `docs/rules/`, `../{{DOCS_REPO}}/GLOSSARY.md`.

## Workflow
- Pick an issue labelled `ready-for-agent` or `ready-for-human`; branch from `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`; PR with `Closes #n`. Never push to `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`.
- Contract-first: types and calls follow `{{API_CONTRACT}}` (skills `consume-api`, `add-page`).
- No secrets, `.env` files or personal data in commits, issues, PRs or AI chats. Nothing secret in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.

## Commands
```sh
npm ci
{{LINT_CMD}}
{{INTEGRATION_CMD}}
{{TEST_CMD}}
{{BUILD_CMD}}
```

## CI gate
One required job runs lint, typecheck, test and build; deploy/release workflows reuse it so no image is built or deployed unless it passes in the same run.

## Editing agents
Edit only `agents/<name>.md`, run `python3 scripts/sync-agents.py`, commit generated files.
